1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,400
一只裹满泥巴的鸡，是乞丐发明的
A mud-caked chicken, invented by a beggar.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,900
清代常熟，叫花子偶得一只鸡
Qing Changshu: a beggar, one stray chicken.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,400
没锅没料，用荷叶黄泥裹住
No pot, no spice — lotus leaf and clay.

4
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:09,900
丢进柴火，煨到泥巴变干
Buried in embers till the clay hardens.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,400
剥开泥壳，鸡毛随壳脱落
Crack the shell — feathers peel right off.

6
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:14,900
香气四溢，后来上了宴席
The aroma spread — it reached banquets.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,400
传说皇帝赐名"富贵鸡"
Legend: an emperor named it "Rich Chicken."

8
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:19,900
大盘鸡的江湖，白切鸡的清
Big-plate's swagger, white-cut's calm,

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,400
口水鸡的辣，叫花鸡的土香
spicy drool-chicken, clay-baked earth.

10
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,500
一只鸡，四种中国吃法——你家乡怎么吃？
One chicken, four Chinas — how does yours?
